8a3534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565373 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a9b88805-312e-50ff-a48f-9a2d91e7b91d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565394 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ddd44795-8d4c-547b-9853-d23d19571f47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565452 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186565338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565452 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565452 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565452 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/37/372ac1135e480bcd843f02b05bdeae42d462fccaced8151e4a355d6263d7be64.png)\n\nFind the value of $z$ in the triangle shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565452 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a323077c-5cf0-5ef0-a051-240e1171e494" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565452 #edb/ref 1074 "First, from the diagram, notice that $∠CAB$ and $∠BAD$ are supplementary. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠BAD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB+z & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB & ={180}^{∘}-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle where $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{BC}$, the base angles must be equal:\n\n$$\nm∠C=m∠CAB.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the interior angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠C+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠CAB+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2({180}^{∘}-z)+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {360}^{∘}-2z+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2z & ={220}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565454 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186565394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565454 #edb/ref 1069 "q-21232" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565454 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565454 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/19/19ca38571817d9de8c92de17d5121c33ac1494848766033792dc9586c95fa475.png)\n\nIn the isosceles triangle $△ABC$  with base $\\overset{―}{AB}$, point $E$ lies on the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$, $\\overset{―}{AE}=\\overset{―}{EC}$ and $m∠EAC={40}^{∘}.$ What is the measure of $∠B?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565454 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae1938a1-58ee-571b-a544-d365ce409563" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565454 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Consequently,  the base angles must have equal measure:\n\n$$\nm∠BAC=m∠B\n$$\n\nAlso, since $△CEA$ is an isosceles triangle, we have:\n\n$$\nm∠C=m∠EAC={40}^{∘}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $m∠B$ using the fact that the interior angles of $△ABC$ sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BAC+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+m∠B+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠B & ={140}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={70}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186565373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-21222" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565459 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c6/c62f51c2b029d6b1e24e7f30603c5f34ab5d70d96ed84c5c74de15d4e2e6358e.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $∠D?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b85bf70e-60cf-531c-93a8-54cd5e2b47c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565459 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that $△ABC$ is an equilateral triangle. Consequently, all of the interior angles must be equal to ${60}^{∘}:$ \n\n$$\nm∠A=m∠B=m∠ABC={60}^{∘}\n$$\n\nAlso, since $△CDB$ is an isosceles triangle, the base angles must have equal measure:\n\n$$\nm∠CBD=m∠D\n$$\n\nNotice also that $∠ACB$ and $∠DCB$ are supplementary, therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ACB+m∠DCB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {60}^{∘}+m∠DCB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠DCB & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we calculate $m∠D$ using the fact that the interior angles of a triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D+m∠DCB+m∠CBD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D+{120}^{∘}+m∠D & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠D & ={60}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565501 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186565505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565501 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3970f23e-0d4b-58af-b62e-7ed9157998d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565501 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186565454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565505 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "547a136f-0f45-5073-888d-a69eb3373469" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565505 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186565452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565535 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186565501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565535 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d4131835-327a-579d-bd13-775bb94299f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565535 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186565459 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
